CRASH-08: don't walk a NULL Expression array when closing after an input error

ExpressionCount is counted in the first input pass. When that pass already
found an error (a duplicate ID, an invalid option value), createObjects()
returns before controls_create() allocates Expression[], and controls_delete()
then reads ExpressionCount entries of a NULL array on close: a segmentation
fault in swmm_close() (or swmm_run()) instead of the input error message,
with the report file left empty. Skip the loop when Expression is NULL, as
deleteObjects() does for its own arrays.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-08_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/controls.c b/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
index e423886..d1934cd 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/controls.c
@@ -844,7 +844,8 @@ void controls_delete(void)
 {
     int i;
 
-    for (i = 0; i < ExpressionCount; i++)
+    // --- Expression is NULL if input counting failed before it was created
+    for (i = 0; Expression && i < ExpressionCount; i++)
     {
         mathexpr_delete(Expression[i].expression);
         Expression[i].expression = NULL;
